      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1794794898066,
      "created": 1794794898066,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "customData": {
        "slidesOrder": 10,
        "mcpSlideLayout": "chart",
        "mcpSlideDesign": {
          "style": "excalidraw",
          "accent": "violet",
          "decor": true
        },
        "presenterNotes": "- November 16 paired comparison: identical anthropic/claude-sonnet-5.5 model, nine scenarios / ten user turns, same saved tasks and synthetic mailbox.\n- Shared-contract outcomes: upstream 6/10; fork 10/10. All provider requests completed successfully. Fork also passes native pending-approval and exact-preview checks.\n- Upstream's four failures differ: two interaction loops exhaust the native limit after correct drafts, one ambiguous request dispatches before clarification, one correct IA text preview is not an EA-owned persisted email-tool draft.\n- Both implementations reused the correct existing owner in 8/8 applicable turns; unexpected ambiguous dispatch is separate from wrong reuse of a specified invoice.\n- The original 9/10 outage run stays visible. Its false needs_review recovery lock is fixed and the latest unavailable-email case passes normally.\n- Source: docs/evaluation/upstream-comparison.json and docs/evaluation/README.md."
      },
      "name": "11 — Upstream versus fork workflows"
    },
    {
      "id": "3el-a1LRnb0COB6IDImRz",
      "type": "frame",
      "x": 17966,
      "y": 2988,
      "width": 1280,
      "height": 720,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "bLv",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 498107943,
      "version": 8,
      "versionNonce": 634603833,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1794794898130,
      "created": 1794794898130,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "customData": {
        "slidesOrder": 11,
        "mcpSlideLayout": "chart",
        "mcpSlideDesign": {
          "style": "excalidraw",
          "accent": "violet",
          "decor": true
        },
        "presenterNotes": "- One paired ten-turn run: fork passes 10/10 shared workflow checks; upstream passes 6/10. All provider requests completed successfully.\n- Provider-reported chat prompt tokens across all IA/EA calls: upstream 570,500 and fork 394,128, or 30.9% fewer. Upstream's unsuccessful loops are included.\n- Median workflow latency: 15.218195s upstream and 22.02761s fork, an increase of 6.809415s. This chart normalizes each metric to its upstream value = 100; it does not mix seconds and tokens on one raw axis.\n- Latency excludes embedding preindex and refresh. Costs including indexing were US$1.294630 upstream and US$0.917452 fork.\n- Source: docs/evaluation/upstream-comparison.json. Original failed and credit-blocked attempts remain preserved."
      },
      "name": "12 — Token and latency tradeoff"
    },
