      "customData": {
        "slidesOrder": 9,
        "mcpSlideLayout": "chart",
        "mcpSlideDesign": {
          "style": "excalidraw",
          "accent": "violet",
          "decor": true
        },
        "presenterNotes": "- The source fixture submits 120 distinct EA jobs at simulated time zero; every job lasts one simulated second.\n- Upstream immediate execution runs 120 at once. Production SQLite admission in the fork starts 100 and queues 20.\n- At t=1, the first 100 complete and the queued 20 start; all 120 complete by t=2. Capacity is 100 running and 100 waiting.\n- One execution per EA remains enforced. Each initiating request still has five follow-up stages and twenty submission limits.\n- This tests admission using actual SQLite paths with simulated completions. It excludes real models, network and asynchronous scheduler; it is not measured live throughput.\n- Source: docs/charts/measurements.json; concurrency section."
      },
      "name": "10 — Bounded execution admission"
    },
